            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "The Aurora Student Society celebrated World Happiness Day in the second week of March with a painting activity titled \"Tiny Strokes of Happiness.\" The event brought together over 100 participants, including students, faculty, and staff. Students from the Medical College, School of Nursing and Midwifery, Institute for Educational Development, and Faculty of Arts and Sciences were all invited to express their creativity on canvas."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "\"The purpose of this art activity was to illuminate the path to happiness through creativity,\" explained Roshni Kumari, MBBS-2026, Convener of Aurora. \"As brushes danced across canvases, participants immersed themselves in the joy of expression, discovering the happiness in each brush stroke. Through painting, connections were forged, unity was celebrated, and positivity radiated throughout the event.\""
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Aurora and their \"Tiny Strokes of Happiness\" reminded their fellow students about the power of art to uplift spirits and promote Aurora's objectives of mental well-being and awareness."
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "hard_break"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
